dency among KRAS-mutant lines, no supported MSI-high effect on POLR2A, and no meaningful constructed-marker effects. The most informative next analyses are robustness checks in technically stringent screens for the accepted PTEN-loss/STAT3 contexts (high IFN, high EMT, and high stemness) and for TP53-loss/USP7 in high AXL expression, while retaining active complement/context tests for PTEN-loss/STAT3 under high MYC or high AXL and MSI-high/WRN under TP53 loss. All conclusions remain observational within the supplied dataset and do not establish causality or generalizability.",
