  "narrative": "All returned estimates and intervals are already signed to the registered hypothesis direction. A positive signed estimate supports the registered direction: for direction -1 it corresponds to a more negative dependency score in the exposed group, i.e. stronger dependency; for direction +1 it corresponds to a less negative dependency score, i.e. weaker dependency. I used the approximate run-level 10% population-scale benchmarks already registered: about 0.027 for MDM2, 0.018 for USP7, 0.042 for SMARCA2, 0.009 for NFE2L2, 0.028 for STAT3, 0.030 for WRN, and 0.030 for DHX9. Acceptance requires a clinically meaningful point estimate with an interval that reasonably supports the registered direction; wide intervals crossing null or not excluding clinically meaningful opposite effects remain unresolved. Low-Cas9 robustness: H213 is accepted for TP53 loss with weaker dependency_USP7 in low-Cas9 lines; signed estimate 0.3146, lower 0.1585, far above the USP7 benchmark. H214 is accepted for SMARCA4 loss with stronger dependency_SMARCA2 in low-Cas9 lines; signed estimate 0.7543, lower 0.7119, far above the SMARCA2 benchmark. H215 is accepted for KEAP1 loss with weaker dependency_NFE2L2 in low-Cas9 lines; signed estimate 0.7994, lower 0.7513, far above the NFE2L2 benchmark. H222 is accepted for CDKN2A loss with stronger dependency_MDM2 in low-Cas9 lines; signed estimate 0.1088, lower 0.0458, above the MDM2 benchmark. These acceptances support the robustness of accepted core associations under reduced CRISPR screen potency. Ploidy boundary conditions: H210 is accepted in high-ploidy lines, CDKN2A loss with stronger dependency_MDM2; signed estimate 0.1073, lower 0.0600, above benchmark. H217 is accepted in low-ploidy lines; signed estimate 0.1167, lower 0.0419, above benchmark. Similar effects in both ploidy strata reduce evidence for strong ploidy heterogeneity, although this is not formal homogeneity proof. H218 is accepted for PTEN loss with stronger dependency_STAT3 in low-ploidy lines; signed estimate 0.1931, lower 0.0942, far above benchmark despite exposed n=57. H219 is accepted for TP53 loss with weaker dependency_USP7 in low-ploidy lines; signed estimate 0.4322, lower 0.2901, far above benchmark. H225 is accepted for MSI-high with stronger dependency_WRN in low-ploidy lines; signed estimate 0.7876, lower 0.7367, far above benchmark, although the exposed cell n=33 is small. These extend the accepted core effects to genome-instability contexts but remain dataset-specific associations. MTAP specificity: H223 is unresolved and closed. The interaction of CDKN2A loss with MTAP loss on dependency_MDM2 has signed estimate 0.0600, interval -0.0320 to 0.1517. The point estimate exceeds the MDM2 benchmark, but the interval crosses null and cannot support or exclude a clinically meaningful modifier effect. With the accepted MTAP-intact result, this remains consistent with a CDKN2A/MDM2 association that is not purely explained by MTAP co-deletion, but it does not establish a specific MTAP-dependent mechanism. DHX9 exploratory tests: H212 is unresolved and remains active. BRCA2 loss in high-mutation-burden lines shows signed estimate 0.0071, interval -0.0474 to 0.0615; this is too weak and imprecise to support a clinically meaningful replication-stress effect. H224 is unresolved and remains active. In high-screen-quality, MYC-amplification-negative lines, RB1 loss with weaker dependency_DHX9 has signed estimate 0.0247, interval -0.0092 to 0.0586. The point is close to the DHX9 benchmark and suggestive of the exploratory reversal, but the interval includes null and cannot confirm the effect. These DHX9 findings remain hypothesis-generating. Audit: eligibility filters are pre-specified from predictor, technical, and phenotype variables rather than outcome-derived selection, so outcome leakage is unlikely. The main risk is multiplicity, especially for interactions and small-cell contexts. I therefore required large signed lower bounds exceeding clinical-scale benchmarks before accepting robustness contexts, and interpreted near-null or crossing-null interactions as lack of decisive evidence rather than proof of homogeneity. Validation budget is exhausted, so these are internal discovery associations within the supplied dataset, not evidence of causality, therapeutic vulnerability, or generalizability."
