ion artifact, but mechanism remains unproven. Negative or unsupported findings include direct receptor self-dependencies and several canonical expectations: BRAF V600E did not support dependency_BRAF, EGFR amplification was not accepted as a stable dependency_EGFR effect and validation remained imprecise, ERBB2 amplification was near-null for dependency_ERBB2 and tested STAT3 contrasts, KRAS mutation was not a stable predictor of dependency_KRAS or dependency_RIT1, and MYC amplification did not support dependency_DHX9, dependency_RPL11, dependency_POLR2A, dependency_KIF18A, or the tested dependency_MDM2 context. Canonical TP53 loss did not robustly predict dependency_MDM2, MSI-high did not support dependency_POLR2A after validation, PTEN loss did not robustly modify dependency_KRAS among KRAS-mutant lines after validation, and CDKN2A loss did not support the tested dependency_USP7 direction. Constructed markers D/E/F remain uninformative for dependency_STAT3. Unresolved uncertainty remains for EGFR amplification because the discovery point was positive but imprecise and validation did not resolve it; for the CDKN2A/MTAP interaction on dependency_MDM2; and for the DHX9 panel, where original RB1-loss strong-DHX9 was rejected, the reversed weaker-DHX9 signal is exploratory, BRCA2-loss effects are weak, and MSI-high and stricter BRCA2/RB1-context tests remain unresolved. Interaction near-nulls, especially for very large main effects, should be read as insufficient evidence for a tested modifier rather than proof of homogeneity. The most informative next analysis is H211, testing MSI-high versus non-MSI-high dependency_DHX9 under high screen quality and high Cas9 activity, because it can distinguish whether MSI biology affects DHX9 beyond the very strong WRN association or whether MSI effects are WRN-specific. H226, the strict BRCA2-loss DHX9 test under high mutation burden and high screen quality, is the next highest-priority active test. H224 remains relevant for specificity of the exploratory RB1-loss weaker-DHX9 signal in high-quality, MYC-amplification-negative lines. H201 and H216 are closed as low-priority unresolved exploratory leads, and H212 and H220 are deferred in favor of the stricter H226 and focused H224/H211 analysis."
