  "narrative": "All estimates are interpreted as already signed to the registered hypothesis direction. For direction -1, a positive signed estimate means the exposed group has a more negative CRISPR dependency score, i.e. stronger dependency; for direction +1, a positive signed estimate means a less negative dependency score, i.e. weaker dependency. I continued to use approximate 10%-of-absolute-population-mean clinical-scale benchmarks: about 0.042 for dependency_SMARCA2, 0.030 for dependency_WRN, 0.009 for dependency_NFE2L2, 0.018 for dependency_USP7, 0.027 for dependency_MDM2, 0.028 for dependency_STAT3, 0.025-0.030 for dependency_DHX9, and about 0.025 for dependency_KRAS. Acceptance required a clinically meaningful point estimate and an interval whose lower bound is above the relevant benchmark or otherwise clearly supports a clinically meaningful effect in the registered direction. H235 is accepted: CDKN2A loss among high mutation-burden, high screen-quality lines shows strong dependency_MDM2 with signed estimate 0.130 and lower bound 0.031, just above the MDM2 benchmark despite only 62 exposed lines. This resolves the nearest H227 boundary case, so H227 remains unresolved in its original looser context but is closed as investigation. H237 is accepted: CDKN2A loss among MTAP-loss lines also shows strong dependency_MDM2, 0.165 with lower bound 0.081. This argues against a pure MTAP-intact-specific pattern but still cannot prove mechanism. H238, H239, H241, H243, H244, and H248 are accepted fast-growth context robustness results: CDKN2A/MDM2 0.117 lower 0.036; MSI-high/WRN 0.785 lower 0.722; SMARCA4 loss/SMARCA2 0.766 lower 0.726; KEAP1 loss/NFE2L2 weaker dependency 0.835 lower 0.793; TP53 loss/USP7 weaker dependency 0.413 lower 0.272; PTEN loss/STAT3 0.305 lower 0.171. All are far above their outcome benchmarks, although these are overlapping-sample internal replications rather than independent external validations. H247 remains unresolved and closed: slow proliferation by long doubling time with high screen quality gives a large MDM2 point estimate 0.155 but lower bound 0.018 below benchmark and only 31 exposed lines. The remaining unresolved claims are also closed as low-priority ambiguities. H236 and H245 show an exploratory RB1-loss association with weaker dependency_DHX9 in selected technical contexts, but intervals cross zero and lower bounds are below benchmark. H246 shows a small NF1-loss association with weaker dependency_KRAS in KRAS-wild-type high mutation-burden lines, but the interval is wide and not decisive. From an audit standpoint, eligibility criteria used predictors or technical/phenotype strata rather than the tested outcome, so direct outcome leakage is unlikely. However, growth-rate and screen-quality strata can be correlated with CRISPR screen behavior or may act as selected/collider-like contexts, so these acceptances are descriptive associations within selected subsets, not causal or therapeutic claims. Multiplicity and overlapping samples remain concerns, but the accepted effects are extremely large relative to benchmark and repeatedly direction-consistent. Validation budget is exhausted, so all conclusions remain internal associations in the supplied dataset.",
