t estimate is well above the KRAS benchmark and the interval excludes zero, but the lower bound is slightly below the 10% benchmark, so I keep it unresolved and closed. This is the strongest unresolved candidate in this batch and would merit external replication if validation were still available. H220 tests RB1 loss versus intact for weaker dependency_DHX9 in MYC-amplification-negative lines under high screen quality: signed estimate 0.0388, lower bound 0.0111. The point is above the DHX9 benchmark, but the lower bound is substantially below it and the effect is exploratory; I keep it unresolved and closed.  \n\nThe receptor PI3K-bypass hypotheses were not supported. H255 tests PIK3CA mutation versus wild type for weaker dependency_EGFR in high-quality adenocarcinoma: signed estimate -0.0006 with interval -0.0296 to 0.0284. The point is essentially null and opposite the registered direction; I reject the direction-specific association and close the investigation. H256 tests the same exposure for weaker dependency_ERBB2: signed estimate -0.0066, interval -0.0352 to 0.0221. Again there is no clinically meaningful positive effect; I reject and close.  \n\nH257 tests TP53 loss for weaker dependency_RPL11 in high-quality screens: signed estimate 0.0141, lower bound -0.0112, upper 0.0395. The point is below the RPL11 benchmark and the interval is broad, so there is no basis to accept the ribosomal-stress/p53 hypothesis. I keep it unresolved and close it as a low-priority dataset-specific null/underpowered signal. H258 tests ARID1A loss for additional stronger dependency_SMARCA2 within SMARCA4-loss high-quality lines: signed estimate 0.0158, lower bound -0.0400, upper 0.0716. The main SMARCA4-loss effect is robust, but this incremental ARID1A interaction is not clinically meaningful with current precision; I keep it unresolved and close.  \n\nThe two library-context interaction tests are null in the registered direction. H27 gives an interaction of -0.0198 with interval -